    can do. On Armv8-A without SVE the NEON path is expected and correct.
  - GiB/s counts only unavoidable streams (see bytes_per_call in the source).
  - Compare GiB/s against the device's spec bandwidth to test the
    bandwidth-bound thesis rather than assuming it.Good results. Key findings from the benchmark:
- **fp16/bf16 gated_scan**: essentially identical throughput to fp32 (0.80 vs 0.82 GiB/s) — state conversion is negligible vs inner loop
- **fp16 cumdecay**: faster than fp32 (1.20 vs 1.07 GiB/s) — halved write bandwidth
- **bf16 cumdecay**: slower on A57 (0.55 GiB/s) — software bf16 conversion is per-element scalar; this is an honest finding (hardware bf16 on Armv8.6+ would fix it)

