○ ob-t3b.4 · Evaluate the Tensilica HiFi 5 DSP as a fourth compute engine   [● P3 · OPEN]
Owner: Claude · Type: task
Created: 2026-08-02 · Updated: 2026-08-02

DESCRIPTION

  The CIX P1 has a compute engine the plan has ignored entirely: a Tensilica  
  HiFi 5 DSP, spec'd at up to 32 8-bit MACs for AI (Radxa product page,       
  verified). Tiny next to the NPU's 28.8 TOPS, so this is NOT a throughput    
  play and should not displace CPU/GPU/NPU work.                              
                                                                              
  Why it is worth a bead at all: we already hold the DSP SDK                  
  (dsp_sdk_v0.1_20250704_02), so 'CPU + GPU + NPU + DSP' is a demonstrable    
  four-engine heterogeneity story rather than an aspirational one, which reads
  well against the 25-point WOW criterion. A plausible fit is the elementwise 
  gate chains or the causal conv, which are small and streaming-shaped.       
                                                                              
  Deliberately P3 and stretch-labelled: pursue only if the mapping ADR lands  
  early and the core CPU/GPU path is already measured. First step is cheap -  
  check whether the DSP SDK exposes anything usable for fp16/int8 elementwise 
  work, and record the answer either way in docs/FINDINGS.md.                 



