○ ob-8qt.2 · Reuse KleidiAI i8mm/dotprod matmul micro-kernels for the delta-rule updates   [● P2 · OPEN]
Owner: Claude · Type: task
Created: 2026-08-02 · Updated: 2026-08-02

DESCRIPTION

  Do not reimplement what Arm already ships. 109 of KleidiAI's 185 matmul     
  micro-kernels are usable on Cortex-A720 (neon/dotprod/i8mm families; the 76 
  SME/mopa ones are not, since A720 has no SME). These cover the delta-rule   
  small matmuls.                                                              
                                                                              
  Pick the right packed-GEMM variants for our shapes (key/value head dim 128, 
  16 key heads) and precisions, wire in KleidiAI's LHS/RHS packing functions, 
  and benchmark against a naive intrinsics implementation to confirm the reuse
  actually wins at our sizes - KleidiAI is tuned for larger GEMMs and may lose
  on small per-chunk matmuls, which would itself be worth reporting.          
                                                                              
  Keeps the novel work in this project confined to the three primitives       
  KleidiAI genuinely lacks (causal conv on non-SME, gated prefix product,     
  sequential scan).                                                           



