Type: task
Created: 2026-08-02 · Updated: 2026-08-02

DESCRIPTION

  Write up what we learned about running a novel architecture on this         
  toolchain before broad support exists, including the negative findings. This
  document is the strongest Potential Impact artifact in the repo: it saves   
  the next person weeks.                                                      



NOTES

  PARTIALLY DONE 2026-08-02: docs/FINDINGS.md now exists with four substantive
  sections - NOE op-coverage for GDN (measured), the absence of any linear-   
  attention model in CIX's hub, the Armv9.2 toolchain and KleidiAI coverage   
  audit, and the three verified CPU kernels. What remains for this bead is the
  PROFILING half, which is genuinely hardware-gated: per-layer latency        
  breakdown, whether the ArmReshape/ArmTranspose layout conversions around the
  causal conv are elided later in the pipeline, and per-op NPU-vs-CPU         
  placement from a full cixbuild run.                                         



