DESCRIPTION

  All three GDN kernel families (cumdecay, gated_scan, causal_dwconv1d) and   
  their fp16/bf16 variants iterate over channels independently — the channel  
  loop is embarrassingly parallel. On the Jetson Nano A57 (4 cores) we are    
  leaving 3x throughput on the table.                                         
                                                                              
  Add '#pragma omp parallel for' to the channel loop in each kernel, guarded  
  by '#ifdef _OPENMP'. Build with -fopenmp. This is portable C that benefits  
  every multi-core device in the fleet (Pi5, RK3588, Jetson, Graviton, O6).   
                                                                              
