  --description "The gated_scan kernel processes 4 channels per NEON iteration (128-bit). The A57 has 32 NEON registers and the kernel body uses only 3-4. Processing 8 channels per iteration (2 NEON register groups) doubles work per branch and gives the OoO engine more independent instructions to schedule.

Implementation: unroll the NEON channel loop by 2 (process vi*8 and vi*8+4 in the same iteration). Only for gated_scan and cumdecay (the highest-traffic kernels). Scalar tail and SVE paths unchanged.

