    command: cd /home/j2/OrionsBelt && bd remember "Cross-device fleet comparison (baseline, no optimization, Qwen3.5-4B): RK3588 A76 is 2.6-4.5x faster than A57. RK3588 A55 is 0.9-2.2x SLOWER than A57 despite being newer — the A55 is an in-order 2-wide core, and GDN's serial FMA dependency chain (acc = x + acc*g) severely punishes in-order designs that cannot hide FMA latency. The A57's 3-wide OoO scheduler can overlap loads with the dependency chain. This validates the design choice to target OoO cores (A57, A76) as primary and shows why the Edge AI story is about breadth of OoO Arm cores, not just raw frequency." 2>&1

